<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Gate repair in Dallas usually comes down to one of three faults: the gate has moved (sag, drag, a post that shifted), the hardware has worn (hinges, latch, drop rod), or the automation has failed (opener, sensors, power, remote). Each has a different fix and sometimes a different tradesperson, so sorting out which one you have keeps you from paying for the wrong repair.</p><p>White Rock Fence Co is an advertising site, not a contractor. It does not do the work; it connects Dallas-area homeowners with independent fence and gate contractors who quote the job. This page sets out the failure modes, the equipment classes and what belongs in a written quote, with every price attributed to the firm that publishes it. Call (214) 555-0137 to get started.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Sagging and dragging gates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A gate that scrapes the ground usually has a shifted post, a racked frame or worn hinges. The contractor diagnoses which before touching the hardware.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Hinges, latches and drop rods</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Hardware is the cheapest part of a gate job. One Dallas-area firm lists a latch or hinge fix at $60 to $150.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Openers that stop or reverse</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Photo-eyes, limit settings, batteries, remotes and the power supply are the usual suspects. Ask the contractor to name the one that failed.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Swing, slide and cantilever</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Each class of driveway gate needs different room, posts and foundation work. Compare quotes for the same class, width and opener.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Wood and iron gates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Wood leaves tend to sag over time. Iron leaves are heavier and load the posts and hinges harder, so the post work matters more.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Power, permits and HOA</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Power wiring for an opener is electrical work, so ask who holds the electrical license. Confirm permit and HOA rules before you commit.</p>
      </div>
</div>
